These are protocols that govern Security operations in Cybersecurity as a whole.
CIA Triad- Confidentiality, Integrity, Availability
Confidentiality: Information not available to unauthorized access.
Integrity: Information cannot be modified without permission.
Availability: Information is readily available when needed.

Models used in these principles include;
Bell-La Padula Model... this model focuses more on confidentiality. A strong example for this model is in military operations,[No write down, 
No read-up] i.e Principles are set from the get-go, no new rules are "written down" from the top. 
"No reaad up", information cannot be read up,a low ranking officer cannot read or have access to information that is beyond and above his level

Biba Model...this model focuses more on integrity. "No write up, No read down"...this way information cannot be altered from down to top
and information cannot be read or accessed from top to down. Based on my knowledge, this fits a particular principle I've come across,
Least Priviledge of service, this grants the least permission to individuals to get their job done.
